<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Nightly triage pass over the fleet-alert bucket.
     TEMPLATE, not a loadable plist. __KIPI_REPO__ and __HOME__ are materialized by
     install-plist.sh, the same convention com.kipi.linear-dor uses. A plist that
     hardcodes one home directory is unusable on any other machine and fails
     validate-separation's skeleton sweep (ASK-113 / ASK-191).
     Install: bash q-system/.q-system/scripts/install-plist.sh com.kipi.linear-alert-triage

     WHY THIS EXISTS (codex review of PR #268, major 1). linear-alert-triage.py
     shipped with promote/close as hand-run verbs and no scheduled caller, which is
     the same defect the script was written to fix: a consumer nothing invokes.

     DEPLOYMENT, and it is a real gap, tracked as ASK-1130. Committing this
     template does not install it. `kipi install-jobs` is the call site and it
     globs com.kipi.*.plist, so this job needs no registration, but nothing calls
     install-jobs automatically. After this merges, run `kipi install-jobs` from
     the PRIMARY checkout, never from a git worktree: the installer refuses there,
     because running it from one once repointed every live job at a directory that
     was about to be deleted. Every other kipi job has this same property, and
     ASK-1130 owns the fix.

     FLEET-WIDE ON PURPOSE (codex round 5, major 2). Pinning this to one project
     left every other project's alerts outside the only scheduled consumer:
     measured 2026-08-29, 151 open alert tickets of which just 55 were
     kipi-system, so a single-project pass covered about a third of the bucket
     and the rest stayed exactly as inert as before this job existed. The run
     refuses any issue with no project set, so widening the scope cannot create
     the reachable-by-nobody bucket ASK-839 measured.

     Runs at 02:30, half an hour AHEAD of com.kipi.linear-dor at 03:00, on purpose.
     A promoted ticket carries a real DoR, so the drafter then correctly skips it
     rather than spending one of its 8 nightly slots rewriting one. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.kipi.linear-alert-triage</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string><string>-lc</string>
    <string>cd __KIPI_REPO__ &amp;&amp; ./kipi alert-triage --limit 8 --apply</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key><dict><key>Hour</key><integer>2</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__HOME__/.config/kipi/linear-alert-triage.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__HOME__/.config/kipi/linear-alert-triage.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
